# Static serving and cache policy — overrides the Caddyfile that Railpack
# generates by default (Railpack serves static files with Caddy and prefers a
# Caddyfile found at the project root).
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# --------------------
# Production was sending NO Cache-Control header at all — only ETag and
# Last-Modified. With no explicit policy a browser falls back to heuristic
# freshness, roughly 10% of the age of the document, so index.html could be
# served from cache for hours without ever asking the server. That is what made
# the ?v= query strings only half-work: the versioned asset URLs live inside
# index.html, so if the HTML itself never revalidates, nobody ever learns the
# asset URLs changed.
#
# ROLLOUT ORDER MATTERS
# ---------------------
# Ship this file BEFORE the version it is meant to roll out. Clients still
# holding a heuristically-cached index.html will not see a new deploy until
# their own freshness window expires; once they have picked up `no-cache`
# once, every later release reaches them on the next load.

:{$PORT:3000}

root * {$RAILPACK_STATIC_FILE_ROOT:.}
encode zstd gzip

# HTML always revalidates. Railway already sends a strong ETag, so the usual
# outcome is a 304 with an empty body — cheap enough to do on every load, and
# the only thing that guarantees a release is actually picked up.
@html {
	path *.html /
}
header @html Cache-Control "no-cache"

# The service worker decides which build every other asset comes from, so it
# must never be served stale. A cached worker is the one failure mode that can
# pin an installed app to an old version indefinitely.
@service_worker {
	path /service-worker.js
}
header @service_worker Cache-Control "no-cache"

# Everything else is immutable by construction: assets are requested with a
# ?v=X.Y.Z that changes on every release, so a new build asks for different
# URLs rather than hoping a cached one expired.
@immutable {
	path *.css *.js *.png *.jpg *.jpeg *.svg *.webp *.woff2 *.ico
	not path /service-worker.js
}
header @immutable Cache-Control "public, max-age=31536000, immutable"

header {
	X-Content-Type-Options nosniff
	-Server
}

file_server
